  "articleBody": "Installing marble in your bathroom can be a bit tricky, and there are definitely some common pitfalls to watch out for. First off, skipping proper surface preparation is a huge mistake; your substrate needs to be perfectly flat, level, and stable. Otherwise, you risk cracking or uneven tiles down the line. Another biggie is using the wrong adhesive or grout. You absolutely need a white, non-staining mortar that's compatible with natural stone, and ensure you back-butter larger tiles for full coverage. Rushing the cure time for adhesive and grout is another common error that can lead to problems like efflorescence or a weak bond. Neglecting waterproofing in wet areas is a critical mistake – tile and grout aren't waterproof on their own! Also, don't forget expansion joints where needed, and make sure to seal the marble and grout *after* installation. If you're not experienced with natural stone, it’s really wise to bring in a professional for these delicate jobs.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}